From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:19:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] GS6 patch B (part 2): the air scene's clouds turned on
 the graphics chip (M_CloudTurned), -TheaterSkyChip=0 for the two rooms

LaySky lays AirSky::Chip's table from SkyAside and makes Clouds the chip's one mesh, once; NearClouds stays empty.
DrawSky lays the table again only when the puffs' order goes stale (no turn painted aside, none late, no sweep) and
paints the shadows alone (AirParts::ShadowsAlone: a painter that owns no cloud lays every shadow the far room lays,
point for point, 0.24 ms) when the far room would have. The sky's 5 s clock says the lays, what they sent, the
shadows' paints and the slowest frame. The cloud test checks the shadows alone against the far room's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
